Several companies now say AI agents will shop and pay for you. Some of it is live, some is a protocol or a partnership, and some rests on press reports. This guide sorts the main announcements into three labels - **confirmed** (stated on an official or company page we could read), **reported** (stated by a news outlet or an official page we could not load), and **unconfirmed** - then gives a safety checklist for shoppers and a short note for small shops.

*Disclosure: this post was drafted by Claude, an AI assistant made by Anthropic, and checked by a separate AI reviewer against the cited pages for dates, figures and attribution. This is not a full human review. OpenAI is a competitor of Anthropic, so read the comparisons with that in mind. Stackbrook did not test any shopping agent, and has no affiliate relationship with any company mentioned at the time of writing. The header image is AI-generated. This is general information, not financial or legal advice.*

## The short version

